==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Frenshman}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|French|man}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|Frenchmen}}

# A man of [[French]] [[birth]] or [[nationality]].
#* '''1975''', Sue Helder Goliber, ''The Life and Times of Marguerite Durand: A Study in French Feminism'', p. 128:
#*: The former recommended that all members of the Chamber of Deputies be elected by the <u>scrutin de liste</u>: that they be elected by all Frenchmen of both sexes over 21 years old.
# A [[home-made]] [[tool]] used by [[bricklayer]]s to cut excess [[mortar]] from newly pointed [[brickwork]].
# {{lb|en|UK}} The [[red-legged partridge]].

